Welcome to the Secret Santa generator website's repository.  This ReadMe will explain how to use the site.

On the landing page there is a button labeled "Add Participants".  Upon clicking this button, a section in the page opens with a form.  The fields in this form are simple - participant's name, participant's contact info (email/phone, currently TBD), and previous person.  This page is where you will add each person participating in the secret santa gift exchange for that year.  Be sure to spell their name correctly and enter their contact info correctly as well (validation and spellcheck may be added later).  After filling in the 3 fields, select the "add user" button and you will see them added to a table below the form on the same page.  This table allows you to keep track of who the participants are for that year (mainly to avoid adding someone twice).  Editting and Removing participants from the table will be added later, but this would allow you to update a participant's info and remove them from the event if they decide later on that they cannot participate.  Do note that if the user is removed AFTER the email has been sent out, a new drawing will need to be done and another notification of the pairings will need to be sent out.

Also on the landing page is a button labeled "Pair Participants".  Upon clicking this button, the participants listed in the participants table will be randomly matched with someone who isn't themselves nor is the person listed as their "previous person" in that same table.  The purpose of this is to avoid getting the same person multiple years in a row, for good or bad.  Once the pairings have been made, a message will print stating the pairings are done, and the "Send Notification" button will then become enabled.

Lastly, there is a final button labeled "Send Notification".  This button is only enabled (clickable) after the "Pair Participants" button has been clicked and prints the success message.  Upon clicking this button, the participants listed in the participants table will be notified (either by email or text, currently TBD) about who they got for the event.  This notification message will also include a link to the group's google doc that lists each person's gift preferences and address for shipping (shipping only applies to the participant if the person they're getting a gift(s) for is unable to attend the event in person).
